38 XP d=PE m=D c=M rel=WF-017 | Separate CI and CD as appropriate (green CI does not imply deployment) and use environment protection or approval.
  s: As for FG-M-275ce89ace.
39 CD WF-017~ WF-003~ m=M d=WF k=W | Before considering a pipeline complete verify clean-environment restore, builds, configured tests, no developer-machine dependence, no secret exposure, expected artifacts; clean-environment, developer-machine and artifact checks are not entailed (same as K1 calibration item).
  x: pipeline completion check includes clean-environment restore, no developer-machine-state dependency and production of the expected artifacts
  s: A pipeline reproducing the supported commands on a pre-warmed self-hosted runner passes WF-017; M requires verifying a clean-environment restore before completion.
40 CO WF-010 | Independent read-only review; code-review is the canonical procedure (WF-010).
41 CO WF-011 | Finding priority order (WF-011).
42 CO WF-012~ WF-011~ c=M | Differing from an unadopted pattern is not a violation (no manufactured findings; defects over preferences).
43 CO WF-011 m=MN | Style preferences not elevated above defects (WF-011).
44 CO WF-001~ WF-010~ m=M c=M | The review reads the path-matched rules (applies applicable rules during the canonical review).
45 CO WF-010~ WF-001~ c=M | Establish the review target and read changed plus surrounding code (independent review based on inspected code).
46 CO WF-011~ c=M | Identify changed behavior, error cases, effects and protecting tests (basis for correctness-first review).
47 CO WF-001~ c=M | Read path-matched rules and load specialised technique only where relevant (WF-001 apply applicable rules/skills).
48 CO GOV-001 GOV-008~ | In review, SPECIFICATION.md is authoritative and approved CUSTOM_SETTINGS values are intended behavior.
