50 CO GOV-003 GOV-006 m=MN | Do not weaken specified behavior or introduce unapproved product behavior, incl. string semantics via database/framework defaults (GOV-003, GOV-006).
51 CO GOV-005 GOV-004~ GOV-007~ | An explicitly approved, synchronized detail is not a defect; internal details are not product behavior.
52 CO WF-012 m=MN | No hypothetical findings without a plausible execution path (WF-012).
53 CO WF-021~ m=MN c=M | Tool output is evidence, not authority (WF-021's principle applied to review).
54 CO WF-011 WF-012 | Concrete behavioral problems with plausible execution paths; no invented failures.
